vaporOS NuttX patch: sim-windows-host-layer   (WORK IN PROGRESS -- spike, not used by any board yet)

Problem:   NuttX's simulator cannot be built for a Windows host from Linux (or with
           MinGW/MSYS2) because the build only selects the Windows host layer
           (arch/sim/src/sim/win/) for CONFIG_WINDOWS_NATIVE, which is a cmd.exe
           build environment with backslash paths. Everything else falls back to
           sim/posix/, which needs <sys/mman.h>, <termios.h>, <spawn.h>, ... that
           MinGW does not have. Separately, the win/ layer has fallen behind the
           sim: it lacks sim_testset.c and sim_hostsmp.c, which every sim build
           needs, so it does not even get past dependency generation.
Evidence:  Cross-compiling sim:nsh with x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc from Linux:
             - without this patch: "fatal error: spawn.h: No such file or directory"
               for sim/posix/sim_hostmisc.c (and statvfs.h, mman.h, termios.h)
             - with the Makefile change only: "No rule to make target
               'sim_hostsmp.c'" (then sim_testset.c)
Fix:       (1) arch/sim/src/Makefile: use sim/win for any Windows host that is not
           Cygwin (Cygwin has a POSIX layer), not only WINDOWS_NATIVE.
           (2) win/sim_testset.c: identical to the POSIX one (portable stdatomic).
           (3) win/sim_hostsmp.c: single-CPU stubs. SMP on Windows needs a design
           without POSIX signals as IPIs and is not supported.
Status:    Compiles through dependency generation only. The 64-bit MinGW target
           (x86_64-w64-mingw32) CANNOT work: Windows x86_64 is LLP64 (long is 32 bits)
           and NuttX assumes long is pointer-sized ("Compiler definition mismatch for
           LONG_MAX", wint_t/wctype_t conflicts, hundreds of format warnings). The
           next step is a 32-bit target (i686-w64-mingw32 with CONFIG_HOST_X86), whose
           data model NuttX does support. See docs/windows-sim.md.
Upstream:  (1)-(3) MAYBE, after the Windows build is shown to work end to end. Not
           ready to send: nothing here has produced a running binary.

Apply: git -C ../nuttx apply ../vaporOS/patches/nuttx/sim-windows-host-layer.patch   (setup.sh does this)

diff --git a/arch/sim/src/Makefile b/arch/sim/src/Makefile
index db65fea2dc..6ffc7b78ed 100644
--- a/arch/sim/src/Makefile
+++ b/arch/sim/src/Makefile
@@ -99,8 +99,19 @@ ifeq ($(CONFIG_ARCH_HAVE_FORK),y)
 CSRCS += sim_fork.c
 endif
 
+# The host-side files come from sim/win for any Windows host that does not
+# provide a POSIX layer (Cygwin does). That includes MinGW/MSYS2 builds and a
+# MinGW cross-compile from Linux, which are not "Windows native" build
+# environments (cmd.exe, backslash paths) and so don't set WINDOWS_NATIVE.
+SIM_WINHOST = $(CONFIG_WINDOWS_NATIVE)
+ifeq ($(CONFIG_HOST_WINDOWS),y)
+ifneq ($(CONFIG_WINDOWS_CYGWIN),y)
+  SIM_WINHOST = y
+endif
+endif
+
 VPATH = :sim
-ifeq ($(CONFIG_WINDOWS_NATIVE),y)
+ifeq ($(SIM_WINHOST),y)
   VPATH += :sim/win
 else
   VPATH += :sim/posix
